# Sources support context only; proposals are not source-certified recommendations.
def row(id,topic,known,missing,action,source=CV,status='Proposed — not approved'):
 return dict(id=id,topic=topic,known=known,missing=missing,action=action,source=source,status=status)
sections={
'questions':('Decision questions',[
row('Q01','What is the authoritative NFL dataset?','Several NFL namespaces exist.','Complete independently rechecked, timestamped official game and player observations.','Inventory each field; retrieve official gamebooks and retain exact excerpts, retrieval times and hashes.',NFL),
row('Q02','Are predictions genuinely pregame?','Historical files are available; their existence does not prove pregame availability.','Feature publication times and immutable prediction receipts.','Reject every feature with known_at later than prediction_at; freeze training cutoffs.'),
row('Q03','Can lines be executed?','Research forecasts are not executable quotes.','Official operator odds, timestamps, limits, settlement rules and permission to collect.','Keep price and ROI blank until authorized operator records exist.',NFL),
row('Q04','Who actually replaces an absent player?','Injury report includes practice and game statuses.','Official depth rank, active status, expected role, participation and replacement quality.','Join official team depth charts, transactions and game-day inactives; do not infer a replacement from an injury.',NFL),
row('Q05','Does a strategy improve decisions?','A held-out set reduces training/test leakage risk.','Locked future test outcomes and uncertainty-adjusted baseline comparisons.','Freeze hypotheses, metric, sample/power plan and family of tests before evaluation.'),
row('Q06','Who funds rewards and on what terms?','No funded competition is established by this review.','Budget, eligibility, jurisdiction, anti-gaming policy and approved payout rules.','Use paper-only recognition; block monetary awards pending governance approval.',CV),
row('Q07','Can luck be removed?','Evaluation can overfit the validation set too.','Repeated prospective performance and confidence intervals.','Estimate uncertainty, never claim luck eliminated or guaranteed profit.'),
]),
'suggestions':('Suggestions for review',[
row('S01 · P0','Evidence contract first','Sources differ across inherited dashboards.','Field-level official provenance and data rights.','Recommended first path: build an immutable official-source registry. Acceptance: every populated observation has URL, exact excerpt, as-of time and hash.',NFL),
row('S02 · P0','One NFL entry point','Root dashboard is NBA-focused.','Decision on canonical empirical NFL implementation.','Publish this review hub now; retain old namespaces as historical research, not newly verified findings.',NFL),
row('S03 · P0','Availability and replacement monitor','Official injury report is accessible as a snapshot.','Validated automated feed, team depth charts, inactives and participation.','Propose authorized scheduled collection, change alerts and hard freshness checks. Fail closed on stale or missing evidence.',NFL),
row('S04 · P1','Start with singles','Singles need fewer joint-model assumptions than combinations (design rationale, not a proven edge).','Calibrated outcome distributions and executable prices.','Compare simple rating and team-strength baselines on chronological holdouts before promoting complexity.'),
row('S05 · P1','Prospective shadow leaderboard','Historical rankings can reward selection noise.','Locked strategy versions, prediction ledger and future outcomes.','Rank eligible strategies by preregistered lower confidence bound of baseline-adjusted score; show sample size and uncertainty.'),
row('S06 · P2','Parlays only after joint validation','Pairwise coefficients alone do not establish a multi-leg joint distribution.','Aligned leg outcomes, joint probabilities, operator combination quotes.','Use held-out joint-event calibration, tail stress tests and exposure caps. Never multiply marginals without evidence.'),
row('S07 · P2','Player prop combos last','Replacement roles may change opportunities; this is a hypothesis.','Official per-game usage, role snapshots, full marginal distributions and joint outcomes.','Model shared game pace and role uncertainty; test same-player and same-team overlap before any reward eligibility.',NFL),
row('S08 · P1','Decision change log','This hub separates proposals from implementation.','Human approval of model/data-source changes.','Keep status proposed / approved / rejected / implemented with rationale and version. No suggestion here changes a betting model automatically.'),
]),
'strategies':('Strategies and validation',[
row('T01','Single: team-strength distribution','Research hypothesis only.','Official historical scores, schedule context and holdout evaluation.','Fit home-margin and total distributions using prior-only data; report fair spread, total and win probability with uncertainty.'),
row('T02','Single: replacement-impact signal','Research hypothesis only.','Actual replacement role, prior usage and opponent matchup evidence.','Compare injury-aware model to identical injury-blind baseline; isolate incremental held-out skill.',NFL),
row('T03','Cross-game parlay','Research hypothesis only.','Aligned outcomes and measured cross-game dependence.','Validate joint hit probabilities and expected payoff against recorded operator prices.'),
row('T04','Same-game parlay','Research hypothesis only.','Shared game-state distribution and joint-event calibration.','Simulate conditional outcomes; compare joint predictions with held-out joint observations.'),
row('T05','Player prop combination','Research hypothesis only.','Player usage, role, availability, official game logs and operator settlement.','Fit count/yardage distributions; validate tails and shared opportunities, not just average yards.',NFL),
row('G01','Gate: evidence / rights / freshness','Mandatory proposed gate for all strategies.','Pass evidence.','Fail on missing provenance, permission, pregame timestamps or fresh availability.',NFL),
row('G02','Gate: leakage / reproducibility','Mandatory proposed gate for all strategies.','Pass evidence.','Freeze code, seed, data hash and strategy version; chronological validation with no same-game leakage.'),
row('G03','Gate: calibration / baseline improvement','Mandatory proposed gate for all strategies.','Pass evidence and preregistered tolerances.','Use log loss/Brier for probabilities and distribution scoring for margins; compare with simple baseline.'),
row('G04','Gate: luck / multiple comparisons','Mandatory proposed gate for all strategies.','Power plan, test-family register and untouched prospective outcomes.','Block bootstrap by game/week; adjust for all tried strategies; require improvement interval above zero under frozen rules.'),
row('G05','Gate: joint dependence','Mandatory proposed gate for combinations.','Joint outcomes, coefficients with sample sizes/CIs and joint calibration.','Estimate only on training folds; verify on held-out joint events, including rare-tail sensitivity.'),
row('G06','Gate: economics / stability / governance','Mandatory proposed gate for rewards.','Executable odds, costs, stability by season/role, drawdown limits and funded approval.','No ROI or cash prize eligibility before all applicable gates pass. Missing evidence means blocked, not passed.'),
]),
'injuries':('Availability and replacement tracking',[
row('I01','Observed official snapshot','Week 10 injury page retrieved 2026-11-12; Lucas Patrick: C, Concussion, Did Not Participate In Practice, Out (Commanders).','Report publication time, replacement identity and depth rank.','Preserve this limited excerpt; do not infer starter/backup status or a line adjustment.',NFL,'Verified excerpt — snapshot only'),
row('I02','Observed official snapshot','Same retrieved page: Malik Harrison: LB, Groin, Limited Participation in Practice, Questionable (Giants).','Final active status, role, backup rank and expected snaps.','Questionable is preserved verbatim; no numerical probability assigned.',NFL,'Verified excerpt — snapshot only'),
row('I03','Both offensive and defensive replacement chains','Required schema: team, position, player, depth rank, predecessor, effective_at, known_at, official URL.','Verified rank-1/2/3/4 chains and role evidence.','Leave ranks blank until official team evidence is acquired; never equate roster order with depth rank.',NFL),
row('I04','Deficiency hypothesis','No defensive/offensive deficiency is established here.','Opponent-adjusted impact with sample size and uncertainty.','Test position-specific matchup deltas, shrink small samples and separate role changes from player quality.',NFL),
row('I05','Automated operation','This static site is not a live injury collector.','Authorized collection endpoint, rate policy, durable storage and scheduled monitoring.','Proposed: poll permitted reports, diff versions, reconcile IDs and suppress affected prices if stale. No active live-monitor claim.',NFL),
]),
'flagged':('Flagged for Review',[
row('F01','Third-party NFL inputs','nfl-quant/data/provenance.json lists nflverse and fantasydatapros archives.','Full official row-by-row corroboration.','Do not promote inherited results as official-source-only verified. See linked repository evidence.',NFL,'Needs review'),
row('F02','Inherited NFL freshness','nfl-lab/data/verification_report.json describes an earlier eight-week dataset.','Current official field-by-field re-verification.','Structural checks are not independent external fact verification; do not reuse old lines as current.',NFL,'Needs review'),
row('F03','Injury-policy source returned 404','Attempted operations.nfl.com/inside-football-ops/players-legends/player-health-safety/injury-report-policy/ returned flag-on-play 404 on 2026-11-12.','Current policy text.','Leave policy requirements unverified; use accessible injury page only for observed status excerpts.',NFL,'Needs review'),
row('F04','Correlation and economics not established','No coefficient, price, ROI or performance number is newly certified here.','Officially sourced aligned observations and reproducible calculation.','Values remain blank in the metric register; inherited third-party experiments are context, not verification.',CV,'Needs review'),
row('F05','Rewards and skill claims blocked','No strategy passes the gates in this review.','Prospective evidence and governance.','No funded payouts or guarantee of skill. Randomness cannot be removed from NFL outcomes.',CV,'Needs review'),
row('F06','Repository audit scope','Read coordination, workflow files and selected NFL source/provenance/model reports.','Independent line-by-line factual recheck of every inherited namespace.','This is a bounded audit, not certification of the entire repository. Preserve unrelated work.',NFL,'Needs review'),
])}
nav=[('index','Overview')]+[(k,v[0]) for k,v in sections.items()]+[('metrics','Metrics & leaderboard'),('sources','Sources & audit')]
css='''*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f3f6fa;color:#17283a;font:16px/1.55 system-ui}header,main,footer{max-width:1320px;margin:auto;padding:24px}header{background:#102c42;color:white;max-width:none}header>div{max-width:1272px;margin:auto}nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}nav a{padding:7px 12px;background:#fff;color:#143952;border-radius:6px}a{color:#075c85}h1{line-height:1.15}h2{margin-top:28px}.notice{background:#fff5d9;border-left:5px solid #b67c00;padding:18px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr));gap:16px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #d8e2e9;padding:20px;border-radius:10px}.scroll{overflow:auto}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;background:white;font-size:14px}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:14px;border:1px solid #d8e2e9}th{background:#e5eef5}caption{text-align:left;padding:12px 0}button,input{padding:10px;font:inherit}input{width:min(100%,480px);margin:16px 0}footer{font-size:14px}a:focus,input:focus{outline:3px solid #db9700}'''
(P/'style.css').write_text(css)
def page(name,title,body):
 links=''.join(f'<a href="{k}.html"'+(' aria-current="page"' if k==name else '')+f'>{e(t)}</a>' for k,t in nav)
 (P/(name+'.html')).write_text(f'<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>{e(title)} · NFL Decision Desk</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"></head><body><header><div><p>OWN4 / NFL RESEARCH GOVERNANCE</p><h1>{e(title)}</h1><nav aria-label="Main">{links}</nav></div></header><main>{body}</main><footer>Reviewed 2026-11-12 UTC · Snapshot, not live odds or wagering advice. Blank means unverified, not zero. Sources support only their stated scope. <a href="../index.html">Repository dashboard</a> · <a href="flagged.html">Flagged for Review</a></footer></body></html>')
for key,(title,rows) in sections.items():
 body='<p class="notice">Proposals require review before implementation. Source links support context, not profitability or approval. No missing fact is inferred.</p><label for="filter">Filter this table</label><input id="filter" type="search" placeholder="Search topic, missing evidence, status…"><div class="scroll"><table><caption>'+e(title)+' — evidence and next actions</caption><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th scope="col">'+h+'</th>' for h in ['ID / status','Question or topic','Known / bounded finding','Missing information','Discovery / acceptance action','Official reference'])+'</tr></thead><tbody>'
 for r in rows:
  body+='<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+e(x)+'</td>' for x in [r['id']+' · '+r['status'],r['topic'],r['known'],r['missing'],r['action']])+f'<td><a href="{r["source"]}">Official reference</a></td></tr>'
 body+='</tbody></table></div><script src="filter.js"></script>'
 page(key,title,body)
(P/'filter.js').write_text("document.getElementById('filter').addEventListener('input', function(){const q=this.value.toLowerCase();document.querySelectorAll('tbody tr').forEach(r=>r.hidden=!r.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(q));});\n")
page('index','NFL Decision Desk','''<p class="notice"><strong>Executive decision: research-only.</strong> Do not activate betting strategies or cash rewards. This review does not establish profitable lines, live replacement tracking, or skill independent of luck.</p><div class="cards"><article class="card"><h2>1 · Evidence first</h2><p>Official injury excerpts are checked. Complete pregame datasets, depth chains and price histories remain missing.</p><a href="questions.html">Questions and missing answers →</a></article><article class="card"><h2>2 · Review before change</h2><p>Eight prioritized suggestions with acceptance criteria. Recommended path: evidence contract → singles → prospective test → combinations.</p><a href="suggestions.html">Review suggestions →</a></article><article class="card"><h2>3 · Reward skill cautiously</h2><p>All candidates blocked pending gates. Prospective calibration and baseline improvement come before ROI claims.</p><a href="strategies.html">Strategies and gates →</a></article></div><h2>Executive summary</h2><p>The repo contains multiple NFL implementations, while the canonical landing page remains NBA-centric. Preserve existing research but do not treat archive-based calculations as newly verified official facts. First acquire timestamped official observations and replacement-role evidence. Then originate probability distributions and fair lines with uncertainty, validate chronologically, and compare against simple baselines. Only evaluate economics when recorded, executable operator prices and settlement rules exist.</p><p>Pairwise correlation does not specify a multi-leg joint probability. Same-game and prop combinations need separate joint calibration. Statistical testing can quantify uncertainty; it cannot eliminate luck or guarantee profitable bets.</p><h2>Existing NFL work — not re-certified</h2><ul><li><a href="../nfl/index.html">NFL framework</a></li><li><a href="../nfl-lab/index.html">NFL Lab</a></li><li><a href="../nfl-quant/index.html">NFL Quant (contains third-party inputs)</a></li><li><a href="../nfl-research/index.html">NFL research specification</a></li></ul><p><a href="EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY.md">Download executive summary</a> · <a href="review-register.json">Machine-readable review register</a></p>''')
metricrows=''
for name in ['Home win probability','Fair spread / total','Injury adjustment','Same-game correlation','Cross-game correlation','Prop-pair correlation','Joint hit probability','Out-of-sample Brier improvement','ROI','Reward amount']:
 metricrows+=f'<tr><td>{e(name)}</td><td></td><td>Unverified — blocked</td><td>Acquire official observations; preregister calculation and validate before publication.</td><td><a href="{CV}">Official evaluation guidance</a></td></tr>'
page('metrics','Metrics & leaderboard','<p class="notice">No eligible winner is declared. Every candidate is blocked pending evidence. Empty cells are intentional.</p><div class="scroll"><table><caption>Unverified metric register</caption><thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Value</th><th>Status</th><th>Next action</th><th>Reference</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+metricrows+'</tbody></table></div><h2>Proposed reward policy</h2><p>Freeze strategy versions and all attempted hypotheses; accept immutable pregame forecasts only. Separate singles, cross-game parlays, same-game parlays and prop-combo divisions. Rank only gate-passing entries by preregistered baseline-adjusted scoring with game/week-clustered uncertainty. Publish sample size, stability, drawdown and score intervals; no award when evidence is insufficient. Cash rewards require a funded, legally reviewed policy; no budget or payout is invented.</p><h2>Dependence specification</h2><p>Store leg definitions, event and cutoff IDs, aligned sample size, coefficient method, interval, missingness, training window and held-out joint calibration. Estimate binary hit association and continuous forecast-residual correlation separately. A model-derived coefficient is not an official league statistic. For two binary legs, joint probability must lie between max(0, pA+pB−1) and min(pA,pB). For three or more legs, pairwise coefficients do not identify the joint distribution.</p><h2>Fair line specification</h2><p>Fit a pregame joint home/away score distribution on prior data. Win probability is the mass where the selected team wins; fair spread balances cover probabilities accounting for pushes; fair total balances over/under probabilities. State sign conventions and settlement rules. Quotes must come from an operator, not from inferred consensus or fabricated odds.</p>')
page('sources','Sources & bounded audit',f'''<p class="notice">Official links are not blanket verification. Only the two injury excerpts and the inspected evaluation guidance were independently read in this session. No entire-repository factual certification is claimed.</p><div class="scroll"><table><caption>Source inspection, 2026-11-12 UTC</caption><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Read scope</th><th>Limitation</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>NFL injury report</td><td>Week 10 opening section, Commanders/Giants statuses</td><td>Retrieved snapshot; no report publication timestamp or depth-rank evidence. Remaining games not certified.</td><td><a href="{NFL}">NFL official page</a></td></tr><tr><td>scikit-learn cross-validation</td><td>Opening guidance on overfitting, test/validation split and test leakage</td><td>Official software documentation, not NFL strategy efficacy evidence.</td><td><a href="{CV}">Official documentation</a></td></tr><tr><td>NFL policy lookup</td><td>Returned 404 flag-on-play</td><td>No policy provision verified; use injury page for status observations only.</td><td><a href="{NFL}">Accessible official report</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Local audit trail</h2><ul><li><a href="{REPO}nfl-quant/data/provenance.json">Inherited third-party provenance</a></li><li><a href="{REPO}nfl-lab/data/verification_report.json">Inherited structural verification report</a></li><li><a href="{REPO}COORDINATION.md">Coordination and deployment record</a></li><li><a href="verify.py">This hub’s structural verifier</a></li></ul><p>Local validation checks table-row reference coverage, missing metric values, navigation and deterministic generation. It does not prove external facts or crawl every outgoing URL.</p>''')
(P/'review-register.json').write_text(json.dumps(sections,indent=2)+'\n')
(P/'EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY.md').write_text('''# NFL executive summary — 2026-11-12

Decision: research-only. No newly certified profitable strategy, empirical correlation, executable line, ROI or cash reward.

Recommended sequence: official timestamped evidence and usage rights → verified injury/depth/active roles → simple singles model → locked prospective evaluation → joint-outcome models → governance-approved rewards.

The current NFL injury page was read for two bounded player-status excerpts. Starter/backup rank and replacement impact remain unknown. The attempted policy URL returned 404. Existing nfl-quant inputs include third-party archives; existing model results are not re-certified as official-source-only facts. Root navigation is NBA-focused.

Suggestions are proposals, not approvals. All strategy candidates must pass evidence, leakage, calibration, multiplicity, dependence and economic/governance gates. Luck cannot be eliminated. Missing coefficients and prices remain blank. The static dashboard does not provide continuous injury monitoring or execute bets.

Sources inspected: https://www.nfl.com/injuries/ (opening Week 10 section); https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/cross_validation.html (opening overfitting and held-out evaluation guidance).

See questions.html, suggestions.html, injuries.html, strategies.html, metrics.html and flagged.html for discovery actions and acceptance requirements. Audit scope is bounded to the new hub and selected inherited reports; no claim that every legacy fact is independently verified.
''')
